WEBVTT

00:00:19.125 --> 00:00:19.958
Ikkun.

00:00:19.958 --> 00:00:21.375
Are you awake?

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:24.625
Where are we right now?

00:00:24.625 --> 00:00:26.708
We just left Nagoya.

00:00:26.708 --> 00:00:27.792
We'll be in Kyoto soon.

00:00:27.792 --> 00:00:32.042
Aw, I wanted to check the
choreography for the new song,

00:00:32.042 --> 00:00:33.875
but I didn't get a chance to do anything.

00:00:33.875 --> 00:00:36.583
You're tired, so it couldn't be helped.

00:00:36.583 --> 00:00:39.833
Yeah, you should sleep when you can.

00:00:39.833 --> 00:00:42.625
Us out-of-town students use up a lot of energy

00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:45.708
just commuting to Tokyo.

00:00:45.708 --> 00:00:49.167
But I have a track meet coming up,

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:51.958
so I want to focus on Procella
as much as I can right now

00:00:51.958 --> 00:00:55.333
before my time gets taken up by practice.

00:00:55.333 --> 00:00:59.417
Oh, are you talking about how you were
chosen to run in the 400m dash?

00:00:59.417 --> 00:01:02.417
Then, don't you think it's even more important
not to push yourself too much right now?

00:01:02.417 --> 00:01:04.750
But I promised!

00:01:08.583 --> 00:01:10.042
Ikkun?

00:01:12.333 --> 00:01:13.708
Are you all right?

00:01:13.708 --> 00:01:14.708
Yeah...

00:01:14.708 --> 00:01:17.750
Jeez, you should tell us if you're injured.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:19.958
Then we can help you.

00:01:19.958 --> 00:01:21.208
Sorry.

00:01:21.208 --> 00:01:23.500
I hurt it yesterday during club activities.

00:01:25.333 --> 00:01:27.500
How's Iku's foot?

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:28.625
Kai.

00:01:28.625 --> 00:01:33.125
Right now, Mr. Kurotsuki
is explaining to all the staff.

00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:36.667
It looks like we'll restart
filming at a later date.

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:38.542
I'm sorry, I--

00:01:38.542 --> 00:01:41.875
It was okay since we were
just filming a music video,

00:01:41.875 --> 00:01:44.792
but if we were on stage, we wouldn't
have been able to take it back,

00:01:44.792 --> 00:01:48.333
and it could've turned into a bigger accident.

00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:49.458
Yes, sir.

00:01:49.458 --> 00:01:54.708
Iku, which is more important to you?
Track, or being an idol?

00:01:54.708 --> 00:01:56.083
Huh?

00:01:56.083 --> 00:01:58.625
We're getting more work as Procella.

00:01:58.625 --> 00:02:05.250
I think it'll be really hard to both be
an idol and do your club activities.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.667
If something like this happens again...

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:09.000
It's fine!

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.000
I'll make sure what happened
today doesn't happen again!

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:17.042
I'll definitely show you I can be
an idol <i>and </i>stay on the track team!

00:02:17.042 --> 00:02:20.250
Iku Kannaduki never goes back on his word!

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:23.583
...is how I feel, but...

00:02:23.583 --> 00:02:24.875
Ikkun...

00:02:24.875 --> 00:02:26.958
Don't worry so much about it!

00:02:26.958 --> 00:02:31.417
But at this rate, it looks like
I won't be able to do either well...

00:02:34.458 --> 00:02:36.833
I'm such a failure...

00:02:36.833 --> 00:02:42.208
Other high school students are better
at doing a bunch of other stuff.

00:02:42.208 --> 00:02:43.875
For example...

00:02:43.875 --> 00:02:48.708
Hajime and Haru seem like they've been
invincible since their high school days.

00:02:48.708 --> 00:02:49.625
That's true.

00:02:49.625 --> 00:02:55.500
From what I heard, those two were
at Japan's most prestigious school

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.750
and maintained top-class grades.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:03.792
Haru was part of the student council and
was respected by students and faculty alike.

00:03:03.792 --> 00:03:04.042
"Student Council"

00:03:04.042 --> 00:03:06.000
"Student Council"
Haru's always been good

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.167
at looking after others, huh?

00:03:08.167 --> 00:03:12.750
Apparently, Hajime was also scouted
by the student council as a first year--

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.250
As a first year?!

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:18.083
--but he wasn't interested, so he refused.

00:03:18.083 --> 00:03:21.250
Even so, many were drawn to his charisma,

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:24.708
and it looks like he was always
surrounded by an entourage.

00:03:24.708 --> 00:03:27.500
That's straight out of comic books!

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:31.083
Our Kai in Procella doesn't lose to them, either.

00:03:31.083 --> 00:03:34.000
In high school, he was apparently
the captain of a champion soccer team

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.167
and even went to nationals, remember?

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:38.500
Oh, I heard about that, too.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.042
He was even scouted for a professional team!

00:03:41.042 --> 00:03:44.167
I wonder what kind of high schooler Shun was...

00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:50.042
I don't really know, but I'm sure
he wasn't a normal high schooler.

00:03:50.042 --> 00:03:51.958
Yeah...

00:03:51.958 --> 00:03:55.000
Arata and Aoi are
third-year high schoolers like us,

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.375
but they don't seem to be having a hard time.

00:03:57.375 --> 00:04:00.167
"Ladies and gentlemen, we will"
Huh? Aoi might not be, but Arata is just

00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:04.042
"soon make a brief stop at Kyoto."
kind of spacey and does things at his own pace.

00:04:04.042 --> 00:04:06.750
Anyway, just do your best at the track meet.

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:11.875
But we have an overnight job before it,
so we might not be able to go cheer you on.

00:04:11.875 --> 00:04:13.875
Sorry, Ikkun.

00:04:13.875 --> 00:04:16.125
Don't worry about that!

00:04:16.125 --> 00:04:17.417
See you later!

00:04:17.417 --> 00:04:18.500
Bye.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:19.917
See ya.

00:04:24.375 --> 00:04:25.833
It's not just me.

00:04:25.833 --> 00:04:29.875
Everyone else is an idol and
a student at the same time, too.

00:04:29.875 --> 00:04:32.792
I have to work harder!

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:37.333
"Glasswork Heart"

00:04:37.333 --> 00:04:39.542
"Glasswork Heart"
Morning classes, done.

00:04:39.542 --> 00:04:41.167
You seem tired.

00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:43.000
Are you okay, Kannaduki?

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.375
Oh, uh, yeah.

00:04:45.375 --> 00:04:48.125
You go back and forth between here and Tokyo

00:04:48.125 --> 00:04:50.500
all while going to school
and being on the track team.

00:04:51.458 --> 00:04:54.458
But Ikkun's the energetic
character in Procella, right?

00:04:54.458 --> 00:04:56.250
It's remarkable how you always keep smiling!

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:58.750
Huh? Um...

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:02.833
Yeah. Please keep supporting Iku Kannaduki!

00:05:02.833 --> 00:05:04.250
Just kidding.

00:05:05.375 --> 00:05:08.292
Who can say anything to a smile like that?

00:05:13.833 --> 00:05:15.375
You.

00:05:15.375 --> 00:05:16.792
Yoru.

00:05:21.333 --> 00:05:23.375
Thinking about something?

00:05:23.375 --> 00:05:25.208
You look a little spaced out.

00:05:25.208 --> 00:05:27.333
Yeah, well...

00:05:27.333 --> 00:05:29.958
Are you worried about Ikkun?

00:05:29.958 --> 00:05:34.917
Because the always positive Ikkun
seemed a little down yesterday?

00:05:34.917 --> 00:05:37.083
I'm worried, too.

00:05:37.083 --> 00:05:41.792
Even if we worry, he's the only one
who can resolve his problems, right?

00:05:41.792 --> 00:05:43.542
That's true, but...

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:49.833
All we can do is support him
as much as we can as he worries.

00:05:49.833 --> 00:05:53.583
We can't do more than that,
and we have no obligation to.

00:05:55.375 --> 00:05:56.792
You're right.

00:05:58.833 --> 00:06:00.208
Yum, this is good.

00:06:00.208 --> 00:06:02.792
You're cooking's the best after all, Yoru.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:05.375
"Lacrosse National Championships"
You're just saying that.

00:06:09.583 --> 00:06:12.333
<i>Tsukiuta Radio</i>, also known as <i>Tsukiradi</i>...

00:06:12.333 --> 00:06:14.083
...is about to begin!

00:06:15.042 --> 00:06:18.333
Hello, new and returning listeners!

00:06:18.333 --> 00:06:20.750
I'm Iku Kannaduki from Procellarum.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:23.583
I'm Rui Minaduki from Procellarum.

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:24.958
Thanks for listening.

00:06:24.958 --> 00:06:29.708
This is <i>Tsukiuta Radio</i>, a live radio
show hosted by Rui and me.

00:06:29.708 --> 00:06:31.583
We're starting this week's show now!

00:06:31.583 --> 00:06:33.083
Our guests are--

00:06:33.083 --> 00:06:34.792
Hey, good evening.

00:06:34.792 --> 00:06:38.500
I missed you, all you girls in
the world who are in love with me.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:39.958
It's me, your dear Shun.

00:06:39.958 --> 00:06:42.708
This isn't broadcast around
the whole world, though.

00:06:42.708 --> 00:06:44.917
I'm Kai Fuduki, and I'm
in charge of taking care of Shun.

00:06:44.917 --> 00:06:46.333
Thanks for tuning in.

00:06:47.333 --> 00:06:51.417
Well then, why don't we
move onto the first segment, Rui?

00:06:51.417 --> 00:06:53.500
Okay, let's go.

00:06:57.625 --> 00:06:59.583
Hey, Ikkun.

00:06:59.583 --> 00:07:02.000
Shun, good work today!

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.000
Kai's not with you?

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:08.458
Kai is buying delicious tea for me right now.

00:07:08.458 --> 00:07:11.625
Rui and I have some time before
our next recording session, too,

00:07:11.625 --> 00:07:14.083
so we were going to go buy pudding
at the convenience store.

00:07:14.083 --> 00:07:16.333
Do you want anything?

00:07:16.333 --> 00:07:20.250
Nope. But there <i>is </i>something
I'd like to give <i>you</i>.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:21.250
Huh?

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:23.000
"Iku"

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:26.583
A good luck charm to help
you do well at the track meet.

00:07:26.583 --> 00:07:30.292
Did you make this yourself, Shun?

00:07:30.292 --> 00:07:33.417
Of course. It's filled with magic.

00:07:33.417 --> 00:07:34.375
What?!

00:07:34.375 --> 00:07:39.125
So that a miraculous wind will
blow when you start running.

00:07:39.125 --> 00:07:43.500
And so the measuring instrument will
malfunction when you cross the finish line

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:46.667
and give you a few extra seconds.

00:07:46.667 --> 00:07:50.500
S-Stop that! I'll win with my own ability!

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:52.917
I'm kidding.

00:07:52.917 --> 00:07:56.250
You're so honest, it's amusing, Ikkun.

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:59.917
It's hard to think of it as a joke when
<i>you're </i>the one talking about magic, Shun.

00:08:01.833 --> 00:08:03.500
Thank you.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.417
Even if there's no magic in it, it feels

00:08:05.417 --> 00:08:06.167
like there's some amazing power in this.

00:08:06.167 --> 00:08:08.417
"Iku"
like there's some amazing power in this.

00:08:08.417 --> 00:08:11.417
"Iku"
After all, it's handmade by you!

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:16.667
Oh, sorry! I've gotta go.

00:08:16.667 --> 00:08:18.333
Thank you very much!

00:08:21.625 --> 00:08:23.125
I'm back, Shun.

00:08:23.875 --> 00:08:25.667
Oh, Iku?

00:08:26.708 --> 00:08:28.792
Did you give him the good luck charm?

00:08:28.792 --> 00:08:29.875
Yeah.

00:08:29.875 --> 00:08:34.292
Oh, I forgot to tell him
you helped make it, too.

00:08:34.292 --> 00:08:38.083
Huh? I pricked my fingers working on that, too!

00:08:38.083 --> 00:08:40.500
While you were elegantly drinking your tea.

00:08:41.458 --> 00:08:45.500
But Ikkun was happy, you know.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:47.333
Was he?

00:08:47.333 --> 00:08:49.333
Then, I'm glad.

00:08:49.333 --> 00:08:52.583
He'll win his race, right?

00:08:52.583 --> 00:08:55.250
I hope so.

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:57.875
What are you trying to say?

00:08:57.875 --> 00:09:00.750
Lost lambs cannot run fast

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:04.125
because they do not know
where they are going.

00:09:04.125 --> 00:09:06.750
They must be especially careful at night

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:09.208
because it's dark,
so they can become depressed.

00:09:09.208 --> 00:09:12.917
I think that's the state Ikkun is in right now.

00:09:14.125 --> 00:09:18.958
Oh, did what I say the other day
make him feel pressured?

00:09:18.958 --> 00:09:21.958
I want to tell him not to worry about it,

00:09:21.958 --> 00:09:24.958
but if he seriously wants to continue
both track and being an idol,

00:09:24.958 --> 00:09:28.458
then it's a wall he'll have to overcome someday.

00:09:28.458 --> 00:09:32.292
It's not something he wants to hear,
but someone has to say it.

00:09:32.292 --> 00:09:34.333
It's hard being the big brother, huh?

00:09:34.333 --> 00:09:35.750
I guess.

00:09:36.625 --> 00:09:38.958
But, well, I think it'll be fine.

00:09:38.958 --> 00:09:42.042
Because there's magic in that good luck charm.

00:09:42.042 --> 00:09:44.167
That was a joke, wasn't it?

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:46.667
Huh?

00:10:09.875 --> 00:10:12.667
"To Iku
From Koi & Kakeru"

00:10:21.708 --> 00:10:22.792
"Message received."

00:10:22.792 --> 00:10:23.625
"From: You Title: To Iku"

00:10:23.625 --> 00:10:25.625
"From: You Title: To Iku"
Run toward tomorrow!

00:10:48.583 --> 00:10:50.000
I'm home...

00:11:05.917 --> 00:11:07.458
Oh, Rui.

00:11:07.458 --> 00:11:08.875
Ikkun!

00:11:10.292 --> 00:11:11.958
You're still awake?

00:11:11.958 --> 00:11:14.792
Yeah. Were you doing independent practice?

00:11:14.792 --> 00:11:17.250
Yup! Tomorrow's the day of the track meet.

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:19.375
I have to do my best.

00:11:19.375 --> 00:11:22.792
Ikkun, you're making
a different sound from usual.

00:11:22.792 --> 00:11:23.792
Huh?

00:11:23.792 --> 00:11:26.833
Oh, could it be this?

00:11:26.833 --> 00:11:28.625
It has a bell.

00:11:28.625 --> 00:11:31.375
Shun gave it to me as a good luck charm.

00:11:31.375 --> 00:11:34.083
Oh, You and Yoru sent me a message, too.

00:11:34.083 --> 00:11:36.708
I <i>have </i>to do well tomorrow!

00:11:36.708 --> 00:11:38.292
"Do well"?

00:11:38.292 --> 00:11:39.583
You mean, win?

00:11:39.583 --> 00:11:42.333
Well, that would be best, but...

00:11:42.333 --> 00:11:45.542
I just want to be satisfied with how I run.

00:11:45.542 --> 00:11:52.000
And someday, I want to live up to everyone's
expectations and become an amazing runner.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:53.875
It's the same for being
an idol and working, too.

00:11:56.625 --> 00:12:00.958
But sometimes I think I can't do it.

00:12:00.958 --> 00:12:05.125
Am I being too greedy for
wanting to work hard at both?

00:12:05.125 --> 00:12:07.250
Am I dreaming too much?

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:11.542
Thinking about that makes
my running steadily worse.

00:12:12.583 --> 00:12:15.792
I think it's okay even if you don't run well.

00:12:15.792 --> 00:12:17.125
Huh?

00:12:17.125 --> 00:12:19.500
Kai said to me before--

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:24.125
Because I don't know about the world,
and I have no stamina,

00:12:24.125 --> 00:12:29.208
I wondered if it was okay for me
to just depend on Kai.

00:12:29.208 --> 00:12:35.125
Kai said, "Rui, you have things only you can do,

00:12:35.125 --> 00:12:38.208
so it's okay if there are things you can't do.

00:12:38.208 --> 00:12:42.042
Just slowly increase the things you <i>can </i>do.

00:12:42.042 --> 00:12:45.292
That's why the rest of us are here."

00:12:48.875 --> 00:12:53.750
It's okay if we can't do it yet--
if we're still working at it.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.417
Let's work hard together.

00:12:55.417 --> 00:12:56.708
Rui...

00:12:56.708 --> 00:12:58.542
I see... together...

00:12:58.542 --> 00:13:00.458
We just have to work hard together.

00:13:00.458 --> 00:13:03.167
We're Procella's twin pair, after all!

00:13:03.167 --> 00:13:04.333
Huh?

00:13:04.333 --> 00:13:07.750
If Procella were a family,
then Kai would be the dad,

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:13.167
Yoru would be the mom, You's the big brother,
and we're the twins. Right?

00:13:13.167 --> 00:13:15.958
Shun's... a mystery, though.

00:13:17.083 --> 00:13:19.750
If I'm with you, Rui, I feel like I can do it.

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:22.292
Everyone's cheering us on, too.

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:25.292
Yeah.

00:13:25.292 --> 00:13:28.542
Oh yeah, what do you dream of doing, Rui?

00:13:28.542 --> 00:13:29.917
I'll cheer you on!

00:13:29.917 --> 00:13:31.333
Huh?

00:13:35.667 --> 00:13:37.458
I won't tell you yet.

00:13:37.458 --> 00:13:40.625
Why not? Come on, tell me!

00:13:40.625 --> 00:13:42.583
Because... it's embarrassing.

00:13:42.583 --> 00:13:44.458
Oh, I see.

00:13:44.458 --> 00:13:45.500
Sorry.

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:50.208
But when I'm up to telling people,
you'll be the first one I tell.

00:13:50.208 --> 00:13:53.000
My... dream...

00:13:55.042 --> 00:13:57.750
Okay! Thanks, Rui!

00:14:15.833 --> 00:14:19.083
Hey, no chasing each other inside the dorms!

00:14:19.083 --> 00:14:21.125
Oh no, I'm gonna be late!

00:14:29.417 --> 00:14:30.542
Where's Ikkun?

00:14:30.542 --> 00:14:32.875
Oh, he left a long time ago.

00:14:32.875 --> 00:14:35.333
Did you forget that his track meet is today?

00:14:35.333 --> 00:14:39.042
I don't have room in my mind
for anything non-work-related.

00:14:39.042 --> 00:14:40.208
Liar.

00:14:40.208 --> 00:14:44.625
Your motto is "If I didn't have to,
I would never work."

00:14:44.625 --> 00:14:47.542
Oh, you know me so well, Kai!

00:14:47.542 --> 00:14:49.000
That's exactly it.

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:52.083
But today, I will go to work.

00:14:52.083 --> 00:14:54.750
Oh, to toil and toil some more.

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:57.000
As long as the world wants me,

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.917
I cannot do as I wish.

00:14:59.917 --> 00:15:05.125
You know you only have the recording for
the music program this afternoon, right?

00:15:05.125 --> 00:15:07.542
What are you being so dramatic about?

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:10.375
That's right.

00:15:10.375 --> 00:15:12.583
I'm looking forward to that.

00:15:13.792 --> 00:15:15.167
Hey.

00:15:16.583 --> 00:15:19.250
This was on the floor.

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:21.542
Oh, is that Iku's?

00:15:21.542 --> 00:15:23.792
Oh no, did he drop it?

00:15:23.792 --> 00:15:25.250
Oh dear.

00:15:26.583 --> 00:15:29.792
Everyone's cheering us on, too.

00:15:29.792 --> 00:15:31.792
Ikkun...

00:15:31.792 --> 00:15:33.667
I'll be back!

00:15:33.667 --> 00:15:36.542
H-Hey, where are you going?

00:15:37.792 --> 00:15:39.542
Looks interesting.

00:15:39.542 --> 00:15:41.458
Maybe I'll go, too.

00:15:41.458 --> 00:15:43.042
Huh? Huh?!

00:15:43.042 --> 00:15:45.250
W-Wait a second, you two!

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:46.667
Wait for me!

00:15:55.500 --> 00:15:56.917
Huh?

00:15:59.875 --> 00:16:03.542
The men's 400m dash is about to begin.

00:16:03.542 --> 00:16:05.708
--Ikkun!
--Runners, please take your places at

00:16:05.708 --> 00:16:07.667
the start line as instructed.

00:16:11.458 --> 00:16:13.125
Oh, that's--

00:16:13.125 --> 00:16:17.458
You're so cruel. I can't believe you
didn't notice that you dropped it.

00:16:17.458 --> 00:16:21.833
Aren't you glad Rui noticed
the sad voice of the bunny?

00:16:21.833 --> 00:16:24.542
Sorry we didn't get here
till right before your race.

00:16:24.542 --> 00:16:27.042
We should've arrived earlier,

00:16:27.042 --> 00:16:30.792
but all machines seem to hate Shun...

00:16:40.917 --> 00:16:44.250
Sorry, I just imagined it a little...

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:46.583
Thank you for bringing it.

00:16:46.583 --> 00:16:48.000
Thanks, Rui!

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:51.958
I drew this on the way.
Use this as a good luck charm, too!

00:16:51.958 --> 00:16:54.167
Hm? What <i>is </i>this?

00:16:55.542 --> 00:16:56.292
"To Iku"

00:16:56.792 --> 00:16:59.167
Th-Thanks...

00:17:00.958 --> 00:17:04.292
We will now begin the men's 400m dash.

00:17:04.292 --> 00:17:06.000
Oh, I have to go.

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:07.917
Okay. Do your best!

00:17:07.917 --> 00:17:09.083
Do your best!

00:17:09.083 --> 00:17:10.500
I will!

00:17:15.708 --> 00:17:17.125
On your mark--

00:17:22.667 --> 00:17:24.083
Get set--

00:17:39.292 --> 00:17:43.333
In third place, from Tokyo, Yuki Sato.

00:17:46.958 --> 00:17:51.542
In fourth place, from Osaka, Iku Kannaduki.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:55.917
Aw, he was so close.

00:17:55.917 --> 00:18:00.500
Too bad. Iku practiced hard every day, too.

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:02.917
It's fine.

00:18:04.083 --> 00:18:05.292
It's fine.

00:18:05.292 --> 00:18:08.375
Ikkun and I are both still
trying to reach our dreams.

00:18:08.375 --> 00:18:09.792
Rui...

00:18:10.333 --> 00:18:12.417
Still trying to reach your dreams, huh?

00:18:12.417 --> 00:18:14.333
That's wonderful. Look.

00:18:28.333 --> 00:18:31.792
Shun, hurry! We'll be late for the recording!

00:18:31.792 --> 00:18:34.125
I'll go grab a taxi!

00:18:34.125 --> 00:18:36.083
Okay, thank you!

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:39.208
That was dangerous...

00:18:39.708 --> 00:18:40.792
You, hurry!

00:18:40.792 --> 00:18:42.875
I know already!

00:18:42.875 --> 00:18:44.542
You, Yoru!

00:18:44.542 --> 00:18:48.875
Huh? Don't tell me the track meet's over?

00:18:48.875 --> 00:18:50.292
Huh?!

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:53.208
You two are late.

00:18:53.208 --> 00:18:55.417
You two hurried here to see me?

00:18:55.417 --> 00:18:57.958
Th-That's not how it was...

00:18:57.958 --> 00:19:02.375
Our job before this finished early,
so it was kind of on our way...

00:19:03.417 --> 00:19:06.333
With this, all of Procellarum is here, huh?

00:19:06.333 --> 00:19:07.333
Yeah.

00:19:07.333 --> 00:19:10.292
Yeah! I'm looking forward to the
first performance of our new song.

00:19:10.292 --> 00:19:13.125
If we don't hurry,
we'll be late for the recording!

00:19:13.125 --> 00:19:15.042
Oh, yeah!

00:19:15.042 --> 00:19:16.083
We're getting in!

00:19:16.083 --> 00:19:18.500
Um, we need one more car!

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:21.542
Oh dear. So hurried.

00:19:21.542 --> 00:19:27.667
I'd like to travel more elegantly--like on
the back of an Indian elephant.

00:19:27.667 --> 00:19:29.333
I hope it drops you!

00:19:29.333 --> 00:19:31.250
Everyone, hurry up and get in!

00:19:47.292 --> 00:19:49.167
Ikkun, are you all right?

00:19:49.167 --> 00:19:50.417
Are you tired?

00:19:50.417 --> 00:19:55.792
I'm fine! I mean, I'm tired,
but I feel super energetic!

00:20:03.333 --> 00:20:05.917
Then, we're ready, right?

00:20:05.917 --> 00:20:09.042
We'll flaunt to all our fans around the world--

00:20:09.042 --> 00:20:11.708
our elegant and sweet showtime!

00:20:12.667 --> 00:20:16.250
♪ Fluttering and dancing in the sky ♪

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:22.625
♪ Let our love reach you... ♪

00:20:22.625 --> 00:20:23.375
♪ LOVE, ♪

00:20:23.375 --> 00:20:24.458
♪ LOVE, ♪

00:20:24.458 --> 00:20:25.875
♪ LOVE... ♪

00:20:28.083 --> 00:20:29.917
♪ ohhhh... SAY! ♪

00:20:29.917 --> 00:20:31.333
♪ This heart ♪

00:20:31.333 --> 00:20:33.583
♪ Try and move it ♪

00:20:33.583 --> 00:20:36.708
♪ Look, how should I show you? ♪

00:20:36.708 --> 00:20:37.875
♪ Then together with us ♪

00:20:37.875 --> 00:20:39.292
♪ Let's dance! Take my hand ♪

00:20:39.292 --> 00:20:40.750
♪ hey yeah yeah! ♪

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:42.250
♪ Leave it to me ♪

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:45.167
♪ to escort you! ALL RIGHT! ♪

00:20:45.167 --> 00:20:47.875
♪ As if worrying, the passing rain ♪

00:20:47.875 --> 00:20:51.333
♪ caressed my cheek gently,
so as not to be noticed. ♪

00:20:51.333 --> 00:20:55.292
♪ Jumping over faster than a shooting star ♪

00:20:55.292 --> 00:20:58.750
♪ Reach out your hand! ♪

00:20:58.750 --> 00:20:59.667
♪ let's get LOVE! ♪

00:20:59.667 --> 00:21:01.292
♪ Shout to the moon! (shout!) ♪

00:21:01.292 --> 00:21:02.917
♪ Let your shout ring out! (shout!) ♪

00:21:02.917 --> 00:21:04.083
♪ What's up, what's up? ♪

00:21:04.083 --> 00:21:05.833
♪ Let me hear your voice ♪

00:21:05.833 --> 00:21:07.375
♪ Undo your hair ♪

00:21:07.375 --> 00:21:10.375
♪ Saying goodbye to yesterday ♪

00:21:10.375 --> 00:21:11.375
♪ when my eyes were closed ♪

00:21:11.375 --> 00:21:13.917
♪ A single petal fluttering lightly ♪

00:21:13.917 --> 00:21:15.750
♪ Spit it out, SHOUT! (shout!) ♪

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:17.583
♪ Shout out your feelings! (shout!) ♪

00:21:17.583 --> 00:21:18.333
♪ Isn't it fine ♪

00:21:18.333 --> 00:21:20.500
♪ if nothing is for sure? ♪

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:21.542
♪ wow yeah! ♪

00:21:21.542 --> 00:21:22.042
♪ That's right ♪

00:21:22.042 --> 00:21:23.875
♪ Let's put away the lies ♪

00:21:23.875 --> 00:21:26.583
♪ Let lots of love reach you ♪

00:21:31.083 --> 00:21:33.500
♪ Let lots of love reach you ♪

00:21:43.500 --> 00:21:51.125
<i>The moon that marks the beginning shines</i>

00:21:54.542 --> 00:22:01.750
<i>Plucking many words like drifting clouds</i>

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:10.417
<i>A sorrowful and feeble voice</i>
<i>tinged with lost love</i>

00:22:10.417 --> 00:22:17.167
<i>The first month, embracing his beloved, you</i>

00:22:17.167 --> 00:22:21.833
<i>Flowers of snow flutter and dance as they fall</i>

00:22:21.833 --> 00:22:25.792
<i>They flutter and pile up in my heart</i>

00:22:25.792 --> 00:22:33.458
<i>A single petal of brilliant purple takes you away</i>

00:22:33.458 --> 00:22:41.167
<i>They flutter and dance in the gray sky</i>

00:22:41.167 --> 00:22:48.792
<i>The brilliance of a single petal</i>
<i>stands out in the sky beautifully</i>

00:22:48.792 --> 00:22:56.583
<i>Together with the song</i>
<i>that marks the beginning</i>

00:23:11.958 --> 00:23:13.667
"Episode 3: Going Far Beyond"

00:23:13.667 --> 00:23:15.000
"Episode 3: Going Far Beyond"
As part of the larger plan

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:16.125
"Episode 3: Going Far Beyond"
for promoting our new song,

00:23:16.125 --> 00:23:18.458
"Episode 3: Going Far Beyond"
the Gravi members became store clerks

00:23:18.458 --> 00:23:21.708
"Episode 3: Going Far Beyond"
at an anime store for a day.

00:23:21.708 --> 00:23:26.583
If we're going to do it anyway,
maybe I'll give some suggestions.

00:23:26.583 --> 00:23:30.917
If they use my ideas,
I'm sure it'll be a fun event.

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:36.167
Next time, "Going Far Beyond."

00:23:36.167 --> 00:23:42.102
I, Haru Yayoi, will do my best
as manager for a day!
